// App manifest — a name → real-ESM-import map (the synthetic-view import map).
//
// SAIL stays ignorant of what these names MEAN. `ship` and `api` are the
// conformance app's custom data clients (declared here so the conformance
// views can resolve `ship.demo.todos()` and `api.demo.clock()` against real
// ESM imports, type-checked by tsgo). The view-host handles `route` and
// `navigate` are NOT here because DECK injects them into the manifest on its
// own build path (`deck_core::host_context::host_context_clients`) — there is
// no convention fallback in the compiler; a name resolves through the
// manifest or not at all. This map is
// what REPLACES the reserved-word `BUILTINS`/ambient-ctx mechanism:
// composition by real import, type-checked by tsgo, the compiler unaware
// that "ship", "api", or "route" exist.
//
// `construct: true` means the import is a factory (`makeShip()` →
// `ShipClient`), so the synthetic controller emits
// `const ship = makeShip()`.
{
  "clients": {
    "ship": { "from": "@app/clients/demo", "import": "makeShip", "construct": true },
    "api": { "from": "@app/clients/demo", "import": "makeApi", "construct": true }
  }
}
